infographic compare-quadrant-quarter-simple-card
data
  title Four ways to stabilise plans across deploys — only one is the default
  desc One axis: keep the planner adaptive vs pin it hard. The further you pin, the worse a default it makes.
  compares
    - label Statistics-first — the production default
      desc Right for ~90% of cases. ANALYZE in every deploy hook, CREATE STATISTICS for correlated columns, auto_explain alerting. Fresh stats let the planner stay correct as data grows — adaptability preserved.
    - label pg_hint_plan pinning — last resort
      desc Right only for the 1-3 stability-critical queries (fixed-SLA, financial reports). Locks the plan shape; trades adaptability for predictability — tomorrow's data can make today's hint wrong.
    - label Disable join reordering — lock-down sledgehammer
      desc join_collapse_limit = 1 forces the written JOIN order. Useful for hand-tuned analytic queries, but global is a sledgehammer; apply per-role, never database-wide, or large OLTP joins miss the optimal order.
    - label External plan cache + custom executor — wrong default
      desc Seen only in extreme scale-out. Reinventing planner caching outside Postgres adds operational complexity, breaks tooling, and ages poorly. Use only when no native mechanism suffices — which is rare.
theme
